Thanks for the responses on the Microsoft cc infinite spill errors. I found
another strange quirk, that allowed me to compile conquer:

I used the MEDIUM 286 memory model (-Mm2). The small was too small (barfed
on update.c), and both the LARGE 286 amd (SMALL) 386 produced spills, altho
in different files (the LARGE 286 barfed immediately when make'ing combat.c,
while the 386 spilled on navy.c).

The MEDIUM model worked all the way thru the make. I'll try the suggested
fixes involving register declarations. Seems like much of compiling is the
art of fiddling with different features, try try again, til it works....

